💻 Software Installation (Windows)
1. Mission Planner Setup
Download: Mission Planner Latest

Install: Run .exe with admin rights

Configure:

Select COM port (check Device Manager)

Set baud rate to 57600

2. Orange Pi 5 Pro Setup
Step 1: Flash Ubuntu
Use BalenaEtcher to flash Ubuntu Server 22.04 to SD card

Boot Orange Pi and connect via:

Ethernet (for SSH)

PuTTY (for terminal access)

Step 2: Install Dependencies
bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y python3-pip git v4l-utils libportaudio2
pip3 install opencv-python pyserial pyaudio pymavlink dronekit tensorflow
🔗 Connecting Orange Pi to Mission Planner
Method 1: MAVProxy Forwarding
On Orange Pi:

bash
mavproxy.py --master=/dev/ttyAMA0 --baudrate=57600 --out=udp:192.168.1.100:14550
Replace 192.168.1.100 with your Windows PC IP

In Mission Planner:

UDP → Add connection → Port 14550

Method 2: Telemetry Radio
Connect SiK Radio to:

Pixhawk TELEM2 port

Orange Pi USB port

In Mission Planner:

Select COM port of the radio

🚀 Sensor Configuration (Windows + Orange Pi)
1. reCamera Setup
bash
# On Orange Pi via PuTTY:
v4l2-ctl --list-devices
python
# Test script (camera_test.py)
import cv2
cap = cv2.VideoCapture(0)
while True:
    ret, frame = cap.read()
    cv2.imshow("Frame", frame)
    if cv2.waitKey(1) == ord('q'):
        break
cap.release()
2. TFMini LiDAR
bash
# Enable UART on Orange Pi:
sudo raspi-config  # Interface Options → Serial → Disable shell
sudo reboot
python
# Distance reading (lidar_test.py)
import serial
ser = serial.Serial('/dev/ttyS0', 115200)
while True:
    data = ser.read(9)
    if data[0] == 0x59 and data[1] == 0x59:
        print(f"Distance: {data[2] + data[3]*256} cm")
